From d68f75f2c38caa8d2e983d5b1319672eaf299061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Pablo=20Barham=20Alz=C3=A1s?= <pablobarhamalzas@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:46:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] codex-swapper mod: per-model request_non_streaming +
 orphan-delta lifecycle synthesis

ox-alpha (stealth preview on the opencode-go gateway) advertises chat
completions but also serves /responses. Its SSE stream is degenerate on
both gateway bases: bare response.output_text.delta events with no
output_item lifecycle and a response.completed whose output array is null,
so assistant text was dropped ("OutputTextDelta without active item");
with tools attached only an output_item.added announcement arrives and the
arguments never stream, making tool calls unusable.

Two fixes:
- core: synthesize an assistant-message item lifecycle around orphan text
  deltas as a safety net for any similarly broken upstream.
- new ModelInfo catalog flag request_non_streaming: POST once without
  stream and materialize the JSON response into the same event flow
  (Created -> OutputItemDone* -> Completed with usage). New ResponsesClient
  send_request performs the plain POST.

Verified end-to-end on ox-alpha-free: text turn and real shell tool-call
turn both complete with visible output; deepseek-v4-flash regression clean.

Co-authored-by: ox-alpha <noreply@anoma.ly>
